If now {A} is prime, then that which was proposed is done.

But if it is composite, then some prime number measures it. [!just VII.31]

Therefore any number either is prime or is measured by some prime number.

Therefore, *any number is either prime or is measured by some prime number.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
